# A ball with a 2-limb center that contains the intersection of two such balls (milestone2.md, "One
# enclosure interface", "Hull, intersection and split of balls"): ball_intersection_1 on the
# conversions of two limbs (ball_to_interval_2, interval_intersection_2, interval_to_ball_2). If an
# operand is the whole line the other is returned as it is, by the tests of the radii; the selects
# choose the composition when neither operand is the whole line (nx, ny). An empty operand gives the
# empty set through the conversions, and so do two balls whose intervals do not meet. Not claimed:
# that the result is inside X or Y, nor that it is empty whenever the balls are disjoint.
kernel:        ball_intersection_2
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
input:         cy = cy0 cy1
input:         stored ry
output:        cz = cz0 cz1
output:        rz
requires:      ball cx rx
requires:      ball cy ry
ensures:       ball_set cz rz intersection x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 3
source:        both balls to intervals, their intersection, back to a ball, on two limbs (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the ball is selected among the conversions and the operands after tests of the radii; ball_set states what comes out for every pair of canonical balls

(xl0, xl1, xu0, xu1) = ball_to_interval_2(cx0, cx1, rx)
(yl0, yl1, yu0, yu1) = ball_to_interval_2(cy0, cy1, ry)
(zl0, zl1, zu0, zu1) = interval_intersection_2(xl0, xl1, xu0, xu1, yl0, yl1, yu0, yu1)
(c0, c1, r)          = interval_to_ball_2(zl0, zl1, zu0, zu1)
wx                   = eq(rx, const inf)
nx                   = not(wx)
wy                   = eq(ry, const inf)
ny                   = not(wy)
ca0                  = select(ny, c0, cx0)
ca1                  = select(ny, c1, cx1)
ra                   = select(ny, r, rx)
cz0                  = select(nx, ca0, cy0)
cz1                  = select(nx, ca1, cy1)
rz                   = select(nx, ra, ry)
